Body:
Actually, also to OpenCode maintainers: This original issue (title + description) sounds a bit like a question.

I want this to be a bug, or at least a feature request. Is it treated like this, what is the current plan? I am also open to opening a new, clearer issue for OpenCode that points out what is needed, and does not ask how users can do it by themselves...

@thdxr @rekram1-node @adamdotdevin

Automated Reproduction Bot: unable to reproduce the claimed error loss on the reported commit (`3cf1cef`).

`Effect.orDie` moves a typed failure to the defect channel; it does not replace or erase the error. A direct runtime reproduction using this repository's installed Effect version:

```ts
const original = new Error("sub-agent sentinel failure")
try {
  await Effect.runPromise(Effect.fail(original).pipe(Effect.orDie))
} catch (error) {
  console.log({
    sameObject: error === original,
    message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),
  })
}
```

Output:

```txt
{ sameObject: true, message: "sub-agent sentinel failure" }
```

The reported commit also preserves the message through the complete model-facing path:

- [`task.ts` converts the failure to a defect](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/3cf1cef7fed55a314b01635a9a2388ef9f257e5e/packages/opencode/src/tool/task.ts#L334-L335).
- [The AI SDK adapter converts rejected tool execution into `tool-error` using `errorMessage(event.error)`](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/3cf1cef7fed55a314b01635a9a2388ef9f257e5e/packages/opencode/src/session/llm/ai-sdk.ts#L249-L260).
- [The processor persists that original error as the failed tool result](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/3cf1cef7fed55a314b01635a9a2388ef9f257e5e/packages/opencode/src/session/processor.ts#L652-L673), which is then included in model history.

The proposed `catchAll(...ToolFailure...)` would not address the stated concern either: the common tool wrapper subsequently applies [`Effect.orDie` to every tool](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/3cf1cef7fed55a314b01635a9a2388ef9f257e5e/packages/opencode/src/tool/tool.ts#L120-L145), and `catchAll` only catches typed failures, not existing defects. `ToolFailure` belongs at the LLM runtime boundary; the native runtime already performs that adaptation.

Closing because the claimed loss of error information is not occurring. If there is a concrete session reproduction that produces a generic message, please open a new issue with the provider, logs, and failing tool result; that would indicate a more specific serialization or adapter bug.
